{
  "intro": "Every Greek you will meet speaks Standard Modern Greek (**κοινή νεοελληνική**), but almost every region once had, and many still have, its own way of speaking. These pages take each dialect in turn: where it is spoken, how it sounds, how its grammar and words differ from the standard, and which events in Greek history (the Hellenistic **Κοινή**, Byzantine frontiers, Venetian and Ottoman rule, the population exchange of 1923) explain the differences. Start with the two overview pages, then read the dialects in any order. Tap any Greek word for its meaning; dialect forms carry their own glosses.",
